*** Setting up the Binlog Server utility environment with telemetry
*** intervals that are outside their permitted ranges: a zero scrape
*** interval (below the minimum) and a grace and history keep interval
*** far above the maximum. The grace interval is large enough that,
*** applied verbatim, it would overflow the report timer and fire
*** immediately; it must instead be clamped so that no report is written.

*** Generating a configuration file in JSON format for the Binlog
*** Server utility.

*** Determining binlog file directory from the server.

*** Creating a temporary directory <BINSRV_STORAGE_PATH> for storing
*** binlog files downloaded via the Binlog Server utility.

*** Starting Binlog Server Utility in background in pull mode.

*** Waiting long enough that an unclamped, overflowing grace interval
*** would already have written a report, then confirming that none was
*** written because the interval was clamped into range.
include/read_file_to_var.inc

*** Sending SIGTERM signal to the Binlog Server Utility and waiting for
*** the process to terminate.

*** Cleaning up.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility storage directory.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility log file.

*** Removing the Binlog Server utility configuration file.
